{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1199680-integrity-zero","id":1199680,"title":"Integrity Zero?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-26T05:58:45-07:00","id":1199680,"title":"Integrity Zero?","content":"So this fun conversation happened over in our CofD LARP club....<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <i><span style=\"color:#B22222\">[Requiem ST] Hey Jess, It's just occurred that there are actually no rules for what to do when a character on the Integrity scale hits Integrity zero. Obviously if it's a PC, that PC is retired as an NPC... but NPCs at Integrity 0 are a thing. Do we just run that as a chance die for all future Breaking Points or something worse?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">[me] From what I can tell, once taking into account the Soul Loss section in the God-Machine Chronicle book and how it deals with Integrity, the bottom end for Integrity is 1; there is no zero.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\">[Requiem ST] Oh, I've found a thing here. Because of how the Integrity system works, Integrity 0 has to be a thing - it's the point at which a human or minor template supernatural no longer suffers Breaking Points and thus is no longer subject to Beaten Down and Surrender. You can't really get Slashers without it.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">[me] Which brings us to note that Slashers wasn't written to 2nd Edition standards. *sigh* Let me poke around on the Onyx Path forums and see what I can turn up.</span></i><br /> -----<br /> <br /> So that being said, I could really use some help on this one. Have I got the wrong of it, and there is a system in place for Integrity Zero? If so, where can I find it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1731-jessilaurn","name":"Jessilaurn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T06:06:48-07:00","id":1199685,"title":"","content":"Only Hunters (and Slashers) can reach Integrity 0. You can read more about how Hunters deal with it <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/revisiting-the-code-hunter-the-vigil/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Regular humans stay at 1 and just amass worse and worse Conditions, but don't become unplayable like Draugr from VtR or the Mad from MtA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T06:08:15-07:00","id":1199686,"title":"","content":"Excellent, and thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> - Jess","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1731-jessilaurn","name":"Jessilaurn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T06:31:53-07:00","id":1199697,"title":"","content":"Yeah, breaking points are just terrible for humans in that condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}